WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.200
- Hey guys, today's date
is March 24th, 2020.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.390
I want you to know that
because all the information

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.890
I'm sharing makes sense
up until this date.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.870
The situation is evolving rapidly,

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.380
so know that things do change.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.970
That being said, one of my
main goals on this channel

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.200
is to beat up on misinformation.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.120
And I've done a "Doctor Fact
Checks Media" video already.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.020
You loved that.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.740
Now I'm doing a "Doctor
Fact Checks Politicians"

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:25.190
because I've seen some
politicians make statements

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:26.940
that are at best, negligent,

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.460
and at times, purposefully inaccurate.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.850
But before we start,
I wanna make a comment

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.650
about ending social distancing.

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.130
This week, the story has moved to how long

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.580
should we be doing the social distancing?

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.499
Is it worth the economic impact

00:00:41.499 --> 00:00:43.960
of closing of small businesses,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.500
people losing their jobs,

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.630
the stock market taking a tumble?

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.310
And it's actually a good question.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.570
We should be asking it.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.240
And doctors like myself should
really be providing answers

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:54.570
in a time of unknowns.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.650
I just watched a panel on
FOX News of President Trump,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.860
Vice President Pence, a few others,

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.990
talking about this exact issue.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.370
President Trump made a statement

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:07.367
where he says, "We should
be getting back to work

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.510
"around April 12th," which is Easter time.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.447
Now many people are asking,
"Is that the wise move to do?"

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.133
We don't know.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.390
We don't know if that's
the right move to do yet.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:19.090
We need to conduct more tests.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:21.240
We need to get doctors on the front lines,

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.240
their equipment that we
need to treat patients,

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:24.690
and we need see what's happening,

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.460
how the situation is evolving.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.650
Making any kind of
prediction now for April 12th

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:30.860
is a full-on guess.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.160
We don't have all the numbers.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.310
We don't know how the
situation's gonna evolve.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.070
So I think we need to pump
the breaks a little bit.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.550
At this very moment, the reason why I say

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.180
the economic losses are still worth it

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.890
because of the worry of run on hospitals.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.510
This isn't a theoretical problem.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.230
Italy's having it right now.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.240
And if we have it here
in the United States,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.940
people are gonna suffer,
not just those who are over

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:54.090
the age of 70.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:55.840
Everyone's gonna pay a toll for this.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.440
What I'd like to see happen
over the next few weeks,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.470
hospitals get more prepared,

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.340
we transform civilian buildings

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.490
like Jacob Javits Center
right around the corner,

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:08.230
hotel rooms in order to
act as impromptu hospitals.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.920
We get personal protective equipment

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.320
and ventilators to hospitals.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.120
See how many people are sick
with proper testing kits.

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.120
And only once we have all this in place

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:17.110
in the next two weeks

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:19.210
can we then start talking about estimates.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.960
Right now, no place for it.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.500
During this Fox News White House panel,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.130
they had three doctors on.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.940
Dr. Sapphire, Dr. Siegel, and Dr. Oz,

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.390
each asking a question
of Vice President Pence

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.430
and President Trump.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.790
Unfortunately, none of them
asked if our politicians

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.930
are afraid of a run on hospitals.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.050
The simple question remains

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.780
what do we do and how do we
prepare for when millions

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.950
of people simultaneously
catch this novel coronavirus?

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:50.570
And even if 1% need ventilator support,

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.030
which is probably more than that,

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:54.310
how can we manage with
not enough equipment?

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.470
How do we manage with
not enough protection

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.120
where health providers are gonna get sick

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.410
and they have to stay home?

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.380
We need to think about
us on the front lines

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.440
and really get President Trump, Pence,

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:06.620
and everyone in the political sphere

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.180
to think about us and how we
need to manage the situation.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.040
All right, let's fact
check some politicians

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.260
making statements about
the novel coronavirus

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.450
that may not be accurate,

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.520
and some that are really dangerous.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:20.060
- The World Health Organization offered,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.970
offered the testing kits
that they have available

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.930
and to give it to us now.

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:25.770
We refused them.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:28.710
- Were testing kits available
that were perfectly fine?

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:31.570
Yes, however, these tests
are largely reserved

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.820
for low-income countries

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.690
that don't have the testing capacity,

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:36.750
don't have the ability
to make their own tests.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.990
In fact, many countries
were making their own tests

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:41.510
and not taking them because
they have the economy

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.343
to do so.

00:03:42.343 --> 00:03:44.440
How would it look if
an economic superpower

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.510
like the US started claiming
these kits for themselves?

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:48.710
Just pretty bad.

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:51.340
I think what really slowed
down our response time

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:54.350
was that the initial test
the CDC sent out were faulty.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:57.110
And second, it took
forever to commercialize

00:03:57.110 --> 00:04:00.060
these tests for private labs
to do this sort of testing.

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.440
Now that that's happening,
where BioReference, LabCorp

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:04.360
are able to do them,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.810
we can get more tests done.

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.993
- We have a drug called chloroquine.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:13.370
A derivation would be hydroxychloroquine.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.650
We think it has very
serious, very good impact

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.830
on what we're talking about
with respect to the virus.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.043
So you'll take a look at that,

00:04:22.043 --> 00:04:23.690
then you can coordinate with us.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.530
But I think to me, that's a game changer.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.230
First and foremost, it's
not a game changer yet, yet.

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:31.410
We like to be optimistic
in the medical community,

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.290
but first and foremost, we
have to be healthy skeptics.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.820
That does not mean we
disbelieve everything we hear.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:38.450
It means that we have to take everything

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:39.350
with a grain of salt,

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:43.210
especially basing it on limited research.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:44.550
The research that we have presented

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.670
thus far is mainly anecdotal research,

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:49.590
meaning stories or
certain compassionate uses

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.460
where we're just using that medication

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.270
in an experimental form.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.530
In fact, there was a recent research study

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.900
that came out combining
hydroxychloroquine,

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:01.250
this anti-malaria
medication with azithromycin

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:03.140
which is an antibiotic medication.

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:06.270
And it found that it decreased
the amount of the virus

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.620
that's present in the nasopharyngeal swabs

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.810
that we use to test for it.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.370
Now this is a very small study.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.870
It wasn't randomized.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.010
The people that got both
drugs were only six.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.840
That's a very small number.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:21.290
So until we do a proper clinical trial,

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.640
and understand exactly what it means

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.860
to have less virus in your nose,

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.110
because what good is it
if you have less virus

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.270
in your nose, but you're still
showing horrible symptoms

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.490
and still having the same outcomes?

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.010
We need more info, that's what I'm saying.

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.940
We need to do more research
before we start calling

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:38.020
it a miracle drug, a game changer.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.830
Because what happens?

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.000
People start taking it unnecessarily

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.410
and get side effects.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.970
All medications have side effects.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.709
In fact, there was a
couple that ended up taking

00:05:47.709 --> 00:05:50.172
some kind of form of chloroquine,

00:05:50.172 --> 00:05:52.950
I think it was to clean
their aquarium or fish tank

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.210
and ended up dying.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.300
Well, the husband died and now the wife

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.040
is in an intensive care unit.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.860
So we need to be very careful
with our language here.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:03.080
Another issue that I'm sure the President

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.640
didn't think about when
he made these statements,

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:08.240
now it's nearly impossible for my patients

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.550
who have been taking hydroxychloroquine,

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.390
brand name Plaquenil, for
lupus or different types

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.820
of autoimmune conditions to get it

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:18.950
because of this rush on pharmacies

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.389
because people think it cures

00:06:20.389 --> 00:06:22.470
or treats the novel coronavirus.

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:23.430
I think at a time like this,

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:25.270
we have to look to the major organizations

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:26.390
to give us guidance.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:29.280
Dr. Fauci cleared up some
of the fact checking there.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.980
The FDA came out and said
they have not FDA approved

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:35.140
hydroxychloroquine to be a treatment.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:37.670
Are we using it some
compassionate use cases?

00:06:37.670 --> 00:06:41.090
Yes, but we have to understand
this is experimental use

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:42.320
only at this time.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:45.160
- This disease could take your life,

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.280
but that's not the scariest thing to you.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:50.510
There's something that
would be worse than dying.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:51.690
- Yeah.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.900
And look, I'm gonna do
everything I can to live,

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.477
but you know, if you said,

00:06:56.477 --> 00:06:58.037
"Are you willing to take a chance?"

00:06:58.037 --> 00:06:59.560
You know, and if I get sick,

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:00.610
I'll go and try to get better,

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:01.870
but if I don't, I don't.

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:03.140
And I'm not trying to think

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.902
in any kind of morbid way, Tucker.

00:07:04.902 --> 00:07:09.550
But I'm just saying that
we got a choice here.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:13.410
And we're gonna be in a total collapse,

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:15.980
recession, depression,
collapse on our society

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.360
if this goes on another several months.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.790
There won't be any jobs to
come back to for many people.

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.100
- The entire interview
sets up a false dichotomy.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.640
We're okay, putting at risk
those above the age of 70,

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.940
or we have the economic
collapse of this country.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:31.230
This is a purely false dichotomy.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:32.770
It's not that simple.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:34.610
There are many choices to be made.

00:07:34.610 --> 00:07:37.740
And it's not about saying this
is gonna take nine months,

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:40.120
or six months, or three
months, or two weeks

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.080
because we don't know.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.590
It's an evolving situation

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:44.050
that we constantly have to monitor

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:45.330
and make changes when appropriate.

00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.780
Now the reason I bring
up the false dichotomy

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.760
is because we need to understand

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.240
that it's not just about those

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:52.710
over the age of 70.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:55.800
If we open the country back up too early,

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.920
the risk isn't just to them.

00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:59.410
It's to all of us.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.930
Not only are 30-year-olds,
20-year-olds, 50-year-olds

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:06.210
still gonna get sick,
some of them severely,

00:08:06.210 --> 00:08:08.190
there's still a death
rate in those people,

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:10.440
but it's gonna happen so quickly

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:12.160
that hospitals like my own,

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:13.500
like the ones in New York City

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.090
are gonna get overrun,

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:17.890
and doctor are not gonna
be able to provide care,

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:21.540
not only to coronavirus
patients, but to everyone.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.910
You're gonna be a 20-year-old
involved in a car accident.

00:08:23.910 --> 00:08:25.240
Those happen all the time.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:26.073
Guess what?

00:08:26.073 --> 00:08:27.630
ICU's full of corona patients.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:28.710
Where are you gonna go?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.800
If you're diagnosed with cancer
and you need an infusion,

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.010
we don't have anymore IV
supplies because we're using them

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.420
on the coronavirus patients.

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:36.580
Where are you gonna go?

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:40.490
This is not just about those
who are over the age of 70.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.840
I encourage Lieutenant Governor
to come to New York City,

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:45.060
take a look at the hospitals.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.260
They're already, here, overcrowded.

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.810
The ICUs are nearly working at capacity.

00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:53.830
We're going through 40 to
70,000 N95 masks a day,

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.950
and that's with the economy shutdown.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.030
Imagine we open it up

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.680
and everybody gets sick at the same time.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.660
Who's gonna take care of these people?

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:01.493
I have no idea.

00:09:01.493 --> 00:09:03.770
Because I'll tell you exactly
what happens if we do that,

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:06.020
we're gonna run out of
equipment, first and foremost.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.080
Doctors are gonna be facing
decisions on who intubate.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:11.640
The 20-year-old who has
no medical problems?

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:13.880
The 30-year-old who has two kids?

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:16.480
The 50-year-old who has
a family, but smokes,

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:19.170
or the 70-year-old who
has many health problems,

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.320
but has been paying into
Social Security and Medicare

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.270
their entire lives.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.760
How do you make that decision?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.400
Healthcare providers
are still gonna be there

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:27.180
on the front lines
'cause that's what we do.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:28.660
We're gonna get sick.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:30.400
We're gonna start losing our lives.

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.690
We're gonna start showing up to work.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.660
And who's gonna be there to
take care of the patients

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:38.060
who need help that are
not coronavirus patients?

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:39.460
I don't have an answer to that.

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:41.587
So it's not as simple as,
"Let's open up the country

00:09:41.587 --> 00:09:42.550
"to save jobs."

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:43.400
We all want that.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.800
We don't want the economy
to collapse as doctors.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:47.900
In fact, something Trump said earlier

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.547
on another press conference is,

00:09:49.547 --> 00:09:51.037
"If doctors just had their way,

00:09:51.037 --> 00:09:52.397
"they'd shut down the entire country

00:09:52.397 --> 00:09:53.550
"for a period of time."

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:56.010
Yeah, maybe in an experiment form,

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.500
but not in real life.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.520
We don't wanna destroy the economy.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:00.840
We wanna make sure that we lose

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.890
the least amount of lives possible,

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:04.620
we keep hospitals up and running,

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.950
and we're able to take
care of as many people

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:09.430
while maintaining a proper economy.

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:13.560
Now can we open up the
country in a few weeks time?

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.830
It's very possible.

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.080
But we need to wait.

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:17.740
We need to get more testing kits done.

00:10:17.740 --> 00:10:19.400
We need to get providers the protection

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:21.140
we need on the front lines,

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.830
and then make evaluations as they come.

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.140
There's no need to go
on national television

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.370
and say something dramatic,

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.440
that you're willing to lay down your life

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.010
for the novel coronavirus
to save the economy.

00:10:31.010 --> 00:10:32.310
'Cause it's a false dichotomy

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.680
and an inaccurate statement.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:37.350
- He's defunded Centers
for Disease Control.

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:39.810
- They've cut the funding for the CDC.

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:40.830
- The reality of the matter

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.380
is that neither of these
statements are true.

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:48.380
In 2019, Trump proposed a cut
of $1.36 billion to the CDC.

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.630
He proposed this cut.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.140
Congress wouldn't let him have.

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:58.140
Instead, they increased the
CDC budget by $261.6 million.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:00.980
For 2020, Trump proposed cutting

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:04.870
the CDC budget by $750 million, bad idea.

00:11:04.870 --> 00:11:06.230
Congress wouldn't let him do it.

00:11:06.230 --> 00:11:09.790
Instead, they signed
a 420 million increase

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.200
to the CDC budget.

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.720
So while yes, Trump has
proposed cuts to the CDC,

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.440
he's tried cutting their budget.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.840
He's never tried to fully defund it,

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.080
and he's never successfully
cut the budget.

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:22.480
In fact, over the last two years,

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:24.130
that budget has gone up.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:26.350
Please, politicians, when you're making

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:28.230
statements like this, tell the full story.

00:11:28.230 --> 00:11:29.993
- [Bryant] The nasal passages,

00:11:31.046 --> 00:11:35.640
and the nasal membranes are
the coolest part of the body.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:38.270
That's why the virus tends to go there

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.570
until it then becomes healthy
enough to go into the lungs.

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:43.450
This sounds really goofy
and it did to me too,

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:44.890
